Jon Wolf:
I'm looking at what they did to "fix" the default restart file and it seems like they just stuck on an array with no values in it. This is what I get from the fixed file:

ncdump -h v2.LR.historical_0101.elm.r.2015-01-01-00000.nc | grep -i endwb
double ENDWB_COL(column) ;
ENDWB_COL:long_name = "col-level water mass end of the time step" ;
ENDWB_COL:units = "mm" ;
ENDWB_COL:interpinic_flag = 1 ;
ENDWB_COL:interpinic_flag_meanings = "1=nearest neighbor, 2=copy directly, 3=skip" ;
ENDWB_COL:_FillValue = 1.e+36 ;
